James requested R logic to create a Lorenz curve and Gini coefficient graph using a dataset containing GDP per capita and population information, specifically asking for columns `Country Code`, year, gdppc, and pop. I provided a function, `make_lorenz`, which filters the data for a selected year, calculates total GDP, cumulative population, and GDP shares, and then plots the Lorenz curve. The function also computes the population-weighted Gini coefficient based on the Lorenz curve data. Finally, I included an example call to the function, demonstrating how to use it with a DataFrame named `df` for the year 2023, returning both the Gini coefficient and the plot.
